## Studio allocations and local releases

Studio bookings and monthly renewals use the tenant's `studios` allocation, or
`default` for unlisted tenants. Archive continues to use the catalog default.
Replay/conflict resolution precedes admission; cancelled reservations free their
units but cannot be booked again under the same ID. Imports still bypass admission
and contribute to tenant/day usage.

Stage just the current Studio allocation for the next shift:

```sh
node replay.mjs stage orchid-quota studio
```

This appends an idempotent Studio ticket to `fixtures/release-queue.json`, preserving
other releases. Omitting the desk retains coordinated staging for both desks.

## Availability diary

```sh
node utilization.mjs publish-calendar fixtures/pilot.json fixtures/diary.json
```

The feed supplies `edition`, `operations`, `subscriptions`, `days` and a `window`
with `service`, `tenant`, `from` and `through` (inclusive ISO dates). Publication
replays **all** operations before selecting subscribed cells for that audience and
window. Each cell contains `cap`, `used`, `available` (clamped at zero) and the new
edition, including days with no bookings. Other diary cells retain their figures
and editions. Reapplying the same feed leaves the diary unchanged.

`preview-calendar FEED DIARY` previews all subscribed cells without writing;
`rebuild-calendar FEED DIARY` merges the full projection without window filtering.
EOF
